ws Scholarships: a $5,000 scholarship from American Society of Landscape Architects for undergraduate college students. Applications are due February 1, 2027 (73 days left), and no essay is listed.</p>\n      <div class=\"sch-actions\"><a class=\"sch-btn sch-btn-primary\" href=\"/app/\">Let Scholarly apply for you</a><a class=\"sch-btn sch-btn-ghost\" href=\"http://www.asla.org\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Apply on the official site</a></div>\n      <dl class=\"sch-facts\"><div><dt>Award</dt><dd><strong class=\"sch-amt\">$5,000</strong></dd></div><div><dt>Deadline</dt><dd><strong>February 1, 2027</strong> <span class=\"sch-pill\">73 days left</span></dd></div><div><dt>Provider</dt><dd>American Society of Landscape Architects</dd></div><div><dt>Who can apply</dt><dd>Open to undergraduate college students.</dd></div><div><dt>Level</dt><dd>College Students</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Open nationwide (no state restriction listed)</dd></div><div><dt>Essay</dt><dd>None listed</dd></div></dl>\n      <p class=\"sch-checked\">Last checked November 20, 2026. Details come from the provider; confirm on the official site before you apply.</p>\n      <section><h2>By the numbers</h2><ul class=\"sch-stats\"><li>The top award is bigger than 68% of the 587 open scholarships on Scholarly that list an amount (the median is $2,000).</li><li>779 open scholarships on Scholarly right now; 289 close before this one.</li><li>399 open scholarships in <a href=\"/scholarships/level/college/\">scholarships for undergraduate college students</a>, worth $1,916,240 combined at their top award.</li></ul>\n        <p class=\"sch-sub\">Source: Scholarly's database of open scholarships, checked November 20, 2026. Award and deadline as listed by <a href=\"http://www.asla.org\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">American Society of Landscape Architects</a>.</p></section>\n      <section><h2>About this scholarship</h2><p>To aid outstanding students who would not otherwise have an opportunity to continue a professional degree program due to unmet financial need; increase the interest and participation of economically disadvantaged and under-represented populations in the study of landscape architecture; and enrich the profession of landscape architecture through a more diverse population. Landscape architecture and design. Applicants must be permanent U.S. citizens or permanent resident aliens who are third, fourth, or fifth-year undergraduates studying landscape architecture at a Landscape Architecture Accreditation Board (LAAB) accredited school. Selection based on exceptional accomplishments over a sustained period of time in works, leadership and management, knowledge, and service.</p><p><a href=\"http://www.asla.org\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Official page on asla.org</a></p></section>\n      \n      <aside class=\"sch-app\">\n    <h2>Apply to this one in a few minutes</h2>\n    <p>Scholarly fills out and submits scholarship applications for you from one profile. You review each one before it goes out. Works in your browser or on iPhone.</p>\n    <div class=\"sch-app-btns\">\n      <a class=\"sch-btn sch-btn-primary\" href=\"/app/\">Let Scholarly apply for you</a>\n      <a class=\"sch-btn sch-btn-dark\" href=\"https://apps.apple.com/app/apple-store/id6761978211?pt=127870522&ct=seo&mt=8\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 384 512\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M318.7 268.7c-.2-36.7 16.4-64.4 50-84.8-18.8-26.9-47.2-41.7-84.7-44.6-35.5-2.8-74.3 20.7-88.5 20.7-15 0-49.4-19.7-76.4-19.7C63.3 141.2 4 184.8 4 273.5q0 39.3 14.4 81.2c12.8 36.7 59 126.7 107.2 125.2 25.2-.6 43-17.9 75.8-17.9 31.8 0 48.3 17.9 76.4 17.9 48.6-.7 90.4-82.5 102.6-119.3-65.2-30.7-61.7-90-61.7-91.9zm-56.6-164.2c27.3-32.4 24.8-61.9 24-72.5-24.1 1.4-52 16.4-67.9 34.9-17.5 19.8-27.8 44.3-25.5 71.9 26.1 2 49.9-11.4 69.4-34.3z\"/></svg><span>Get the iPhone app</span></a>\n    </div>\n  </aside>\n      <section class=